{"black_box_warning":{"current_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current DailyMed label.","fda_source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22565c2126-57ae-4e29-b443-723bbe7e2072%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"],"proposed_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current FDA/openFDA label.","rationale":"The no-boxed-warning conclusion is supported by FDA/openFDA/FDA label sources, but the current cell explicitly relies on DailyMed, which is not permissible for this field under the audit instructions.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect"},"blocking_questions":[],"fact_checks":[{"current_value":"cenobamate","field":"generic_name","proposed_value":"cenobamate","rationale":"FDA labeling, EMA EPAR, and PubMed RCT records identify the active substance/drug as cenobamate.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/ontozry","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31734103/"]},{"current_value":"Ontozry; Xcopri","field":"trade_names","proposed_value":"Ontozry; Xcopri","rationale":"Xcopri is the FDA-approved US product name; Ontozry is the EMA/eMC product name for cenobamate. No evidence suggests either should be a separate generic-drug row.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/ontozry","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/13008/smpc"]},{"current_value":"","field":"alternate_generic_names","proposed_value":"","rationale":"No alternate INN/common generic name was identified. YKP3089 is a development code and is appropriately captured as a PubMed search alias rather than an alternate generic name.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31734103/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01397968"]},{"current_value":"YKP3089","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"YKP3089","rationale":"YKP3089 is used in cenobamate trial titles and ClinicalTrials.gov records.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31734103/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01397968","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01866111"]},{"current_value":"Yes","field":"available_in_us","proposed_value":"Yes","rationale":"FDA approved Xcopri (cenobamate) tablets for partial-onset seizures in adult patients, and current FDA labeling is available.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/appletter/2019/212839Orig1s000ltr.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"2019","field":"year_fda_cleared","proposed_value":"2019","rationale":"The FDA NDA approval letter is electronically signed 11/21/2019. Note: current label highlights list Initial U.S. Approval as 2020, apparently reflecting controlled-substance scheduling/effective marketing timing, but the FDA approval action was in 2019.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/appletter/2019/212839Orig1s000ltr.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Focal","field":"epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"Focal","rationale":"FDA labeling uses partial-onset seizures, which maps to focal-onset terminology; EMA/eMC explicitly use focal-onset seizures.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/ontozry","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/13008/smpc"]},{"current_value":"Tablet","field":"formulations_available","proposed_value":"Tablet","rationale":"FDA label lists oral tablets in 12.5, 25, 50, 100, 150, and 200 mg strengths; eMC lists Ontozry tablets/film-coated tablets.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/13008/smpc"]},{"current_value":"Adults: titrate to 200 mg once daily; may increase to 400 mg/day","field":"typical_doses_per_day","proposed_value":"Adults: titrate to 200 mg once daily; may increase to 400 mg/day","rationale":"FDA and eMC labeling support once-daily titration to a 200 mg/day target/maintenance dose, with increases up to 400 mg/day based on response and tolerability.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/13008/smpc"]},{"current_value":"400 mg/day","field":"maximum_approved_daily_dose","proposed_value":"400 mg/day","rationale":"FDA and eMC labeling list 400 mg/day as the maximum daily dose in adults without hepatic dose limitation.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/13008/smpc"]},{"current_value":"100 mg/day showed efficacy in focal-onset RCTs; 200 mg/day recommended maintenance","field":"minimum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"100 mg/day showed efficacy in focal-onset RCTs; 200 mg/day recommended maintenance","rationale":"FDA Study 2 reports statistically significant seizure-frequency reduction for 100 mg/day versus placebo; FDA/eMC dosing recommends 200 mg/day as the target/maintenance dose.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31734103/","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/13008/smpc"]},{"current_value":"50-60 h","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"50-60 h","rationale":"FDA label states apparent terminal half-life is 50-60 hours over 100-400 mg/day.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Liver","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"Liver","rationale":"FDA label states cenobamate is extensively metabolized and describes glucuronidation/oxidation pathways; hepatic impairment substantially increases exposure.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Inhibits CYP2C19; induces CYP3A4, CYP2B6, and UGT pathways","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"Inhibits CYP2C19; induces CYP3A4 and CYP2B6","rationale":"FDA clinical interaction data support increased CYP2C19 substrate exposure and decreased CYP3A/CYP2B6 substrate exposure. Current FDA label also lists in vitro CYP2B6/CYP2C8/CYP3A4 induction and CYP2B6/CYP2C19/CYP3A inhibition, but I did not find FDA-label support for UGT induction.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Inhibitor","field":"filter_enzyme_effect","proposed_value":"Inducer; Inhibitor","rationale":"The row's own enzyme text and FDA label both indicate clinically relevant induction and inhibition effects, so a filter containing only Inhibitor is incomplete.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Precise therapeutic mechanism is unknown; cenobamate reduces repetitive neuronal firing by inhibiting voltage-gated sodium currents and positively modulates GABA-A ion channels.","field":"mechanism_of_action","proposed_value":"Precise therapeutic mechanism is unknown; cenobamate reduces repetitive neuronal firing by inhibiting voltage-gated sodium currents and positively modulates GABA-A ion channels.","rationale":"FDA label directly supports this mechanism wording.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Moderate","field":"mechanism_confidence","proposed_value":"Moderate","rationale":"This is a curator confidence classification, not a directly source-verifiable drug fact. It is consistent with the FDA label statement that the precise therapeutic mechanism is unknown.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"not_applicable","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA label (Xcopri Prescribing Information)","rationale":"The mechanism is supported by FDA labeling; removing DailyMed from the source text makes the row align with the trusted-domain source policy.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA label","field":"mechanism_source_tier","proposed_value":"FDA label","rationale":"The cited mechanism source tier is correct.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Shortens QT interval; contraindicated in familial short QT syndrome","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"Shortens QT interval; contraindicated in familial short QT syndrome","rationale":"FDA labeling states dose-dependent QTcF shortening and contraindicates Xcopri in familial short QT syndrome.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"CNS: somnolence 19-37%, CNS: dizziness 18-33%, constitutional: fatigue 11-24%, ophthalmologic: diplopia 4-15%, cardiac: QT shortening >20 ms 31-66%","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"CNS: somnolence 19-37%, CNS: dizziness 18-33%, constitutional: fatigue 12-24%, ophthalmologic: diplopia 6-15%, cardiac: QT shortening >20 ms 31-66%","rationale":"FDA label Table 4 lists active-dose rates of somnolence 19/22/37%, dizziness 18/22/33%, fatigue 12/14/24%, and diplopia 6/7/15%; FDA QT warning lists QT shortening >20 ms in 31% at 200 mg and 66% at 500 mg.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"NCBI LiverTox anticonvulsants table; Epilepsy Society ASM list; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA label (Xcopri Prescribing Information, accessdata.fda.gov); Drugs@FDA approval letter; FDA/openFDA label API for boxed-warning status; PubMed and ClinicalTrials.gov RCT records; EMA EPAR and eMC SmPC for Ontozry","rationale":"The current source list includes DailyMed and Epilepsy Society, which are not in the allowed trusted-source list for this audit, and it omits the PubMed/ClinicalTrials/EMA/eMC sources needed for RCTs and non-US brand/indication facts.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/appletter/2019/212839Orig1s000ltr.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41144696/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT04557085","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/ontozry","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/13008/smpc"]},{"current_value":"Available in US","field":"filter_availability","proposed_value":"Available in US","rationale":"Supported by FDA approval and current FDA labeling.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/appletter/2019/212839Orig1s000ltr.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Focal","field":"filter_epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"Focal","rationale":"Supported by FDA partial-onset and EMA/eMC focal-onset indication language.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/ontozry"]},{"current_value":"Tablet","field":"filter_formulation","proposed_value":"Tablet","rationale":"Supported by FDA/eMC tablet dosage form descriptions.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/13008/smpc"]},{"current_value":"GABA; Sodium channel","field":"filter_mechanism","proposed_value":"GABA; Sodium channel","rationale":"FDA label supports voltage-gated sodium-current inhibition and GABA-A positive allosteric modulation.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Liver/hepatic","field":"filter_metabolism","proposed_value":"Liver/hepatic","rationale":"Supported by FDA metabolism and hepatic impairment sections.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"QT shortening","field":"filter_qt_effect","proposed_value":"QT shortening","rationale":"Supported by FDA QT shortening warning and pharmacodynamics section.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"CNS; Cardiac; Constitutional; Ophthalmologic","field":"filter_symptom_category","proposed_value":"CNS; Cardiac; Constitutional; Ophthalmologic","rationale":"The categories match the supported adverse-effect facts after correcting fatigue and diplopia percentages.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Current ASM for focal/partial-onset seizures.","field":"status_or_notes","proposed_value":"Current ASM for focal/partial-onset seizures.","rationale":"FDA and EMA/eMC sources support current use for partial/focal-onset seizures in adults.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/ontozry","https://www.medicines.org.uk/emc/product/13008/smpc"]},{"current_value":"05-20-2026","field":"data_most_recently_refreshed","proposed_value":"05-20-2026","rationale":"Refresh date is row metadata rather than a drug fact; it matches the supplied audit date.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"not_applicable","supporting_sources":[]},{"current_value":"05-20-2026","field":"fda_black_box_warning_verified","proposed_value":"05-20-2026","rationale":"Verification date is row metadata; the FDA source text should be updated, but the date itself matches the audit date.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"not_applicable","supporting_sources":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22565c2126-57ae-4e29-b443-723bbe7e2072%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]}],"generic_name":"cenobamate","missing_rcts":[{"pmid":"41230998","proposed_link_text":"Kawai2025|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41230998/","title":"Early response rates with adjunctive cenobamate in uncontrolled focal seizures: Prospective analysis of a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled study in a multinational Asian population.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41230998/","why_relevant":"PubMed-listed randomized controlled trial report from NCT04557085 with placebo comparison during early titration. It is a secondary/prospective analysis of an already listed trial, not a new unique trial; include only if the CSV field captures secondary RCT reports."},{"pmid":"41101116","proposed_link_text":"Wu2025|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41101116/","title":"Efficacy of adjunctive cenobamate by focal seizure subtypes: a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled, multicenter study in a multinational Asian population.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41101116/","why_relevant":"RCT-labeled seizure-subtype analysis of NCT04557085 with placebo comparison. It is not a separate trial from Lee2025; include only if secondary RCT reports are in scope."},{"pmid":"41428177","proposed_link_text":"Yu2025|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41428177/","title":"Efficacy and Safety of Adjunctive Cenobamate in Chinese Participants with Focal Seizure.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41428177/","why_relevant":"Post hoc Chinese subgroup analysis from randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled NCT04557085. It provides RR50/MPC/seizure-freedom values for a subgroup but should not be treated as a separate unique RCT."}],"outcome_checks":[{"current_value":"28.2-39 % (drug minus placebo RR50 differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Chung2020 cenobamate 200 mg/day 28.2%; Krauss2019 cenobamate 400 mg/day 39%)","field":"diff_50_responder_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"28.2-53.4 % (drug minus placebo RR50 differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Lee2025 cenobamate 400 mg/day 53.4%; Chung2020 cenobamate 200 mg/day 28.2%; Krauss2019 cenobamate 400 mg/day 39%)","rationale":"Chung2020 and Krauss2019 differentials are correct. Lee2025/NCT04557085 reports an overall maintenance-phase >=50% responder rate for 400 mg/day of 81.6% versus 28.2% placebo, a 53.4 percentage-point differential, so the current maximum RR50 differential is too low if Lee2025 outcomes are included.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41144696/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12927683/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32409485/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31734103/"]},{"current_value":"Chung2020|28.2|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32409485/|222; Krauss2019|39|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31734103/|437","field":"plot_diff_50_responder_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"Lee2025|53.4|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41144696/|519; Chung2020|28.2|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32409485/|222; Krauss2019|39|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31734103/|437","rationale":"Plot values should include Lee2025 RR50 differential if the row includes Lee2025 as outcome evidence.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41144696/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12927683/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32409485/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31734103/"]},{"current_value":"31-74.1 % (drug minus placebo MPC differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Lee2025 cenobamate 400 mg/day 74.1%; Chung2020 cenobamate 200 mg/day 34.1%; Krauss2019 cenobamate 400 mg/day 31%)","field":"diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"31-74.1 % (drug minus placebo MPC differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Lee2025 cenobamate 400 mg/day 74.1%; Chung2020 cenobamate 200 mg/day 34.1%; Krauss2019 cenobamate 400 mg/day 31%)","rationale":"Lee2025 reports -100.0% at 400 mg/day versus -25.9% placebo, differential 74.1. Chung2020 reports 55.6% versus 21.5%, differential 34.1. Krauss2019/FDA Study 2 reports about 55.3% versus 24.3%, differential 31.0.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41144696/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32409485/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31734103/","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Lee2025|74.1|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41144696/|519; Chung2020|34.1|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32409485/|222; Krauss2019|31|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31734103/|437","field":"plot_diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"Lee2025|74.1|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41144696/|519; Chung2020|34.1|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32409485/|222; Krauss2019|31|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31734103/|437","rationale":"The plotted MPC differential values match the cited RCT/outcome evidence.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41144696/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32409485/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31734103/","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"19.5-49.8 % (drug minus placebo seizure-freedom differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Lee2025 cenobamate 400 mg/day 49.8%; Chung2020 cenobamate 200 mg/day 19.5%)","field":"diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"19.5-49.8 % (drug minus placebo seizure-freedom differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: Lee2025 cenobamate 400 mg/day 49.8%; Chung2020 cenobamate 200 mg/day 19.5%; Krauss2019 cenobamate 400 mg/day 20.1%)","rationale":"Lee2025 and Chung2020 values are correct. FDA label also reports Study 2 seizure-free maintenance counts for 400 mg/day and placebo, yielding about a 20.1 percentage-point differential; adding Krauss2019 improves completeness but does not change the displayed range.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41144696/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32409485/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31734103/","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Lee2025|49.8|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41144696/|519; Chung2020|19.5|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32409485/|222","field":"plot_diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"Lee2025|49.8|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41144696/|519; Chung2020|19.5|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32409485/|222; Krauss2019|20.1|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31734103/|437","rationale":"Current plotted Lee2025 and Chung2020 values are supported; Krauss2019 seizure-freedom differential is extractable from FDA Study 2 maintenance-phase seizure-free counts.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41144696/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32409485/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31734103/","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]}],"overall_status":"needs_update","proposed_row_updates":[{"current_value":"CNS: somnolence 19-37%, CNS: dizziness 18-33%, constitutional: fatigue 11-24%, ophthalmologic: diplopia 4-15%, cardiac: QT shortening >20 ms 31-66%","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"CNS: somnolence 19-37%, CNS: dizziness 18-33%, constitutional: fatigue 12-24%, ophthalmologic: diplopia 6-15%, cardiac: QT shortening >20 ms 31-66%","reason":"Correct FDA-label fatigue and diplopia percentages.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/212839s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Inhibits CYP2C19; induces CYP3A4, CYP2B6, and UGT pathways","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"Inhibits CYP2C19; induces CYP3A4 and CYP2B6","reason":"FDA label supports CYP2C19 inhibition and CY